Package: imagonsole
Version: @VERSION@-1
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Piotr Lewandowski <piotr.petexy@gmail.com>
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Depends: @SHLIB_DEPENDS@, libxkbcommon0, libegl1
Recommends: xdg-desktop-portal
Suggests: libvulkan1
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Homepage: https://github.com/Petexy/imagonsole
Description: a photo viewer in the LineXinBar design language
 Shown as Pictures. A folder is a grid of pictures the light travels across. Opening one fills the
 screen with the photograph itself, at its own resolution rather than a
 thumbnail of it, and the pictures either side are read before they are asked
 for — so stepping through a folder shows a photograph rather than a wait for
 one.
 .
 In the viewer a direction pans wherever the picture is larger than the screen
 and steps to the next one where it is not, so nothing has to be switched on
 and the picture itself says what the controls will do. One button walks the
 zoom stops — fit, actual size, twice and four times — while a wheel or a pad's
 triggers zoom by however much they are given. Pictures can be turned, played
 as a slideshow, and read about.
 .
 Photographs are shown the way up the camera held them, and folders are sorted
 the way somebody reads them: nine before ten.
 .
 It is an ordinary Wayland application, drawn in the LineXinBar design language
 and driven from a controller, a keyboard and a pointer at once. It runs under
 GNOME or Plasma as readily as under the shell it was made for.
 .
 libxkbcommon0 and libegl1 are named here because they are opened by name at
 run time rather than linked, so nothing that reads the executable can find
 them. libvulkan1 is only suggested: with a Vulkan driver present this draws
 through it, and without one it falls back to EGL.
